&lt;div data-qa=&quot;job-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;message-list_1791509281.875709&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atomic Machines is building the Matter Compiler™, the first in a new class of AI-native, all-digital manufacturing systems that build working machines directly from code. The Matter Compiler&amp;nbsp; (MC) is aimed at micro-machines: motors and gears the size of a grain of sand, robots small enough to work inside the body, cooling built directly into the chips that run AI, and the many devices like them that have been waiting on a way to build them. Its first product is PrimeSwitch™, an electromechanical power relay the size of a button battery that carries 150 amps continuous current and opens in 50 microseconds, about a thousand times faster than a conventional contactor. Founded by Jeff Holden — serial entrepreneur, ex-Amazon SVP and Uber’s first Chief Product Officer — the company has raised $250 million to date.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atomic Machines is based in the San Francisco Bay Area, with offices in Emeryville and Santa Clara.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About The Role:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a sharp, proactive Accountant to join our lean finance team at Atomic Machines — someone who treats month-end close as a process to be engineered, not just executed. Reporting to the Controller, this role owns the GL close and financial reporting, while also acting as a technical partner in modernizing how our finance data moves — connecting NetSuite, our manufacturing systems, and spend-management tools into live, automated reporting over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Atomic Machines, we are inventing the future of how things are made. In this role, you’ll build the financial foundation for a company revolutionizing micromanufacturing and digital fabrication: clean books, strong controls, and a close process that gets faster and more automated each quarter — by building (and eventually directing AI agents to help build) the pipelines and dashboards that make that possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also work directly with the Controller on the next phase of systems integration and the early build-out of an AI-forward finance function, where agentic tools become part of the team — with the judgment and guardrails to use them responsibly. This role can be based in either our Santa Clara or Emeryville office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own the full month-end close, and build it — over time, not overnight — toward a more automated, AI-assisted state: scoping automation carefully and putting the right guardrails in place so delegation to AI never outpaces the controls around it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the month-end close calendar, coordinating cutoff across AP, payroll, and operations, and build tracking tools that reduce manual chasing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prepare and post journal entries with full supporting documentation; identify good candidates for templated or AI-assisted drafting, with appropriate review steps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Complete key balance sheet reconciliations (bank, prepaid, fixed assets, accrued liabilities, deferred items), moving toward scripted workflows with exception-flagging rather than blind automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prepare the monthly financial statements package for Controller review, including flux analysis and variance commentary, working toward live, auto-refreshing reporting as data pipelines mature.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maintain a clean, audit-ready general ledger, building in automated checks incrementally as you learn where the real risk sits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and maintain data pipelines that pull from NetSuite, manufacturing systems, and spend-management tools into a single source of truth, via scripts, API connections, and AI-assisted tooling — grounded in a real understanding of how NetSuite is configured and how data flows through it, since that’s what makes the automation actually hold up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design live, HTML/dashboard-style reporting that refreshes on current data, working toward a continuous close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scope what should and shouldn’t be automated or delegated to AI&lt;/strong&gt; — knowing the difference between a task that’s safe for an agent and one that needs a human in the loop, and building guardrails (data handling, review gates, audit trail) around every AI-assisted workflow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with the Controller on NetSuite optimization and the next waves of system integration as the business scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to a central data repository for product cost models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support tax and audit preparation by organizing financial data and schedules for external parties.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Need:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3+ years of accounting experience, ideally with manufacturing, hardware, or capital-intensive exposure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real, hands-on comfort with technology beyond Excel&lt;/strong&gt; — you’ve used scripts, APIs, or AI tools to solve a data or reporting problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable using AI tools to build and maintain things&lt;/strong&gt; — even if you’re not a “coder,” you’re unafraid to ask an AI to generate a script, run it, and figure out why it broke.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Good judgment about automation risk&lt;/strong&gt; — you can tell a low-stakes task safe to delegate to AI from a high-stakes one needing human review, and default to building guardrails.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open to growing your technical skillset over time, including basic Python or SQL, as needs evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A first-principles mindset&lt;/strong&gt; — you question assumptions and rebuild processes from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong GAAP knowledge, with working knowledge of leases, debt, equity, revenue recognition, and inventory accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with NetSuite or a similar scaled ERP system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;High ownership and strong communication — able to explain both accounting logic and technical tradeoffs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting or Finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Bonus Points For:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Direct, hands-on NetSuite experience (beyond general ERP familiarity).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience building automation or dashboards with Python, Google Apps Script, or low-code/no-code tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Direct experience using AI coding assistants (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, etc.) or agentic workflows in finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CPA or CPA-track.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Big 4 experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The compensation for this position also includes equity and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$150,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt; Atomic Machines is an equal opportunity employer that values diversity and does not discriminate based on characteristics protected by applicable law. We are committed to an inclusive interview experience, including for individuals with disabilities. To request an accommodation, contact&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:rc@atomicmachines.com&quot;&gt; rc@atomicmachines.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;To help our recruiting team manage application volume and respond to candidates more efficiently, Atomic Machines may use AI-assisted tools. &lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div data-qa=&quot;job-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;message-list_1791509281.875709&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atomic Machines is building the Matter Compiler™, the first in a new class of AI-native, all-digital manufacturing systems that build working machines directly from code. The Matter Compiler&amp;nbsp; (MC) is aimed at micro-machines: motors and gears the size of a grain of sand, robots small enough to work inside the body, cooling built directly into the chips that run AI, and the many devices like them that have been waiting on a way to build them. Its first product is PrimeSwitch™, an electromechanical power relay the size of a button battery that carries 150 amps continuous current and opens in 50 microseconds, about a thousand times faster than a conventional contactor. Founded by Jeff Holden — serial entrepreneur, ex-Amazon SVP and Uber’s first Chief Product Officer — the company has raised $250 million to date.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atomic Machines is based in the San Francisco Bay Area, with offices in Emeryville and Santa Clara.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About The Role:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As COO, you are accountable for turning the Matter Compiler into a manufacturing business. You will set the strategy for and lead the organization that designs, builds, and operates a new generation of fully autonomous commercial fabs, and you will be responsible for delivering the production capacity that Atomic Machines’ growth plan depends on. You will build and lead the leadership team across Manufacturing Engineering, Supply Chain, Shipping/Receiving, Fab Operations, Real Estate &amp;amp; Facilities, Manufacturing Partnerships, Final Assembly &amp;amp; Test, Quality &amp;amp; Reliability, ERP Systems and Foundry Services. You will make the major capital, site, and partnership decisions that determine how fast and how reliably we can scale, including which contract manufacturers we utilize and how much capacity we build in-house versus with partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Matter Compiler enables a truly AI-native fab that is modular, fully autonomous, and 100% digital. Many traditional manufacturing patterns will not apply: the extremely high degree of automation, the high-mix/high-volume interchangeability, the deterministic process control, the real-time nature of the MC, and our approach to input materials. This leader must bring both a deep understanding of manufacturing and operations theory and practice and first-principles thinking, because we are charting significant new territory in advancing humanity’s command of matter. You will define what operational excellence looks like for a kind of factory that has never existed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also lead the People function, including Talent Acquisition, People Partnerships &amp;amp; Organizational Effectiveness, People Operations, and Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits. You will be accountable for the organizational strategy that lets Atomic Machines scale: how we plan headcount against the production ramp, how we structure and level the company, how we pay, and how we keep the hiring bar and culture intact across Santa Clara, Emeryville, and each new fab as it comes online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the executive team reporting to the CEO, you will partner closely with Jeff on company strategy, operating cadence, annual planning and budgets, and represent operations to the board, customers and key partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Manufacturing &amp;amp; Fabs&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the design and operation of our commercial fabs, including all building infrastructure and non-Matter Compiler equipment selection (power, electrical, gas generation and distribution, fluid distribution, cooling systems, layout of MC Lattices and autonomous inbound/outbound systems) as well as all logistics and labor related to fab operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead site selection and build-out so fabs come online on time and in spec relative to forecasted demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own all contract manufacturing relationships for production MC equipment builds and scaling, and extend the CM network by identifying, vetting, and engaging new partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up, operate, and scale our internal Final Assembly &amp;amp; Test function for all MC equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish economic, resilient supply for all materials and components. Own all supplier and OEM relationships, and set and enforce quality and reliability standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage inventory of raw materials, MC components, and finished MC equipment. The real-time manufacturing and generative AI design aspects of the MC challenge norms here.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the framework for managing key manufacturing metrics across the organization: yield, throughput, quality, cost, and uptime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering to enhance and extend the MC’s capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;People &amp;amp; Organization&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own workforce planning tied directly to fab bring-up and the production ramp, so hiring is never the bottleneck on manufacturing capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Talent Acquisition at scale, increasing hiring velocity without lowering the bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design org structure, leveling, and career paths for roles that do not yet exist in traditional manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own compensation, equity, and benefits philosophy and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build manager capability and a performance system that rewards first-principles thinking and ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sustain one Atomic Machines culture across Santa Clara, Emeryville and each new fab as it comes online.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Running the Company&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the leadership team on business process development and deployment, operating cadence, annual planning and budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Atomic Machines is a narrative-based culture, so it is important to be a strong writer who can articulate strategies and initiatives crisply to drive alignment in the organization and to inspire teams, partners, and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate company goals into operating plans with clear owners and metrics and establish strong control loops around key work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a healthy and safe work environment and compliance with federal and state regulations, including employment law.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Need:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years in manufacturing and operations leadership, including executive ownership of highly automated manufacturing at scale and direct experience designing, building, and operating a manufacturing facility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience as a COO, GM, or equivalent executive accountable for multiple functions, ideally at a hardware company scaling from early production to volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or owning the People function, or a track record of building organizations through rapid headcount growth in close partnership with People.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning budgets and capital plans of $100M+ and making major site, capacity, and build-versus-partner decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A robust network and nuanced understanding of the manufacturing industry and its players, with a record of establishing contract manufacturing partnerships at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of hiring and developing strong leadership teams and building operationally excellent cultures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort representing operations to a board, customers, and strategic partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First-principles thinking: starting from a deep understanding of the problem rather than pattern matching to industry norms, and comfort challenging the status quo when the math or physics points to a better way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communicator: articulate, clear, concise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High EQ and real strength in working with people; inspirational and motivational.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS, MS, or PhD in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or another rigorous engineering discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary range starts at $350,000 annually, is based on experience, and includes equity and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt; Atomic Machines is an equal opportunity employer that values diversity and does not discriminate based on characteristics protected by applicable law. We are committed to an inclusive interview experience, including for individuals with disabilities. To request an accommodation, contact&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:rc@atomicmachines.com&quot;&gt; rc@atomicmachines.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;To help our recruiting team manage application volume and respond to candidates more efficiently, Atomic Machines may use AI-assisted tools. &lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div data-qa=&quot;job-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;message-list_1791509281.875709&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atomic Machines is building the Matter Compiler™, the first in a new class of AI-native, all-digital manufacturing systems that build working machines directly from code. The Matter Compiler&amp;nbsp; (MC) is aimed at micro-machines: motors and gears the size of a grain of sand, robots small enough to work inside the body, cooling built directly into the chips that run AI, and the many devices like them that have been waiting on a way to build them. Its first product is PrimeSwitch™, an electromechanical power relay the size of a button battery that carries 150 amps continuous current and opens in 50 microseconds, about a thousand times faster than a conventional contactor. Founded by Jeff Holden — serial entrepreneur, ex-Amazon SVP and Uber’s first Chief Product Officer — the company has raised $250 million to date.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atomic Machines is based in the San Francisco Bay Area, with offices in Emeryville and Santa Clara.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About The Role:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atomic Machines is building autonomous manufacturing systems that combine a core robotics platform with a diverse set of manufacturing processes. As Director of Electrical Engineering, you’ll lead Electrical Engineering in developing electronics and electrical architectures spanning core motion control hardware, sensor/actuator interfaces, and specialized manufacturing systems. You will also lead an Electrical Integration team in defining interconnect strategy and driving interconnect diagrams (ICDs), harness design and procurement, system bring-up, and integration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll organize development across the core robotics platform and manufacturing process portfolio while building a cohesive, scalable electrical architecture. Working proactively with cross-functional partners, the CTO, and EE technical leaders, you’ll uncover needs, align priorities, and balance shared platforms with process-specific designs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape electrical engineering strategy across the core robotics platform and manufacturing process portfolio. Proactively uncover cross-functional needs and translate them into a roadmap, priorities, resource plans, and clear commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a cohesive, scalable electrical architecture across robotics and process systems. Work with the CTO and technical leaders to establish shared platforms and interfaces, balancing reuse with specialized requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive end-to-end delivery. Lead electronics development and electrical integration, including interconnect strategy, interconnect diagrams (ICDs), harness design and procurement, system bring-up, and verification; manage dependencies and adapt plans as requirements evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deep technical leadership. Lead rigorous design reviews, challenge assumptions, and guide engineers through consequential tradeoffs and difficult technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and enforce organization-wide EE standards. Establish consistent practices for design review, documentation, verification, and release, including work outside the core EE team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure robust electrical systems. Address safety, protection, reliability, manufacturability, and serviceability throughout development, including specialized and high-voltage hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop the organization. Hire and coach strong engineers and leaders, delegate ownership, and establish clear expectations for quality and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Need:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep electrical engineering expertise, with the ability to reason from fundamentals, evaluate architecture and detailed designs, and provide credible technical guidance on complex problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering complex electromechanical systems from design through bring-up, integration, validation, and operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of organizing development across varied systems, balancing specialized requirements with shared architecture, reuse, and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive cross-functional leadership: uncovering needs, shaping requirements, developing technical roadmaps, and securing alignment through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and leading strong engineering organizations, including hiring, coaching, developing leaders, managing performance, and delegating ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing engineering standards across distributed teams and driving accountability beyond direct reporting lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s or master’s degree in Electrical Engineering or a related discipline, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Additional Experience We Value:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical engineering leadership in autonomous machinery, robotics, advanced manufacturing, or similarly complex equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and validation of specialized electrical systems for manufacturing or other physical processes, including high-voltage or precision power applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The compensation for this position also includes equity and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$260,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt; Atomic Machines is an equal opportunity employer that values diversity and does not discriminate based on characteristics protected by applicable law. We are committed to an inclusive interview experience, including for individuals with disabilities. To request an accommodation, contact&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:rc@atomicmachines.com&quot;&gt; rc@atomicmachines.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;To help our recruiting team manage application volume and respond to candidates more efficiently, Atomic Machines may use AI-assisted tools. &lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div data-qa=&quot;job-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
