&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Manufacturing Engineer to join our dynamic team. This role contributes directly to operational excellence as we scale into high-volume manufacturing environments — optimizing processes, improving equipment performance, and supporting the design, development, and implementation of manufacturing equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a builder who applies continuous improvement methodologies and can own a well-defined project from concept through implementation into production. As a contributor to our manufacturing operations, you will work with cross-functional teams to help integrate new equipment and processes into the production line while maintaining high standards of quality, efficiency, and safety.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the performance, reliability, and day-to-day sustaining of assigned manufacturing equipment and stations (manual through semi-automated).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support preventive and predictive maintenance activities to minimize downtime and extend equipment life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support manufacturing process development from EVT through DVT and into production ramp on assigned stations/nodes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate engineering BOMs (eBOM) into manufacturing BOMs (mBOM) for assigned assemblies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify bottlenecks, inefficiencies, and quality risks on equipment using data-driven methods; drive improvements in throughput, yield, and cost at the station level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform root cause and corrective action (RCCA), time studies, and risk assessments to resolve production issues and prevent recurrence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate and refine manufacturing standards, including SOPs, work instructions, and training materials, ensuring consistency and process discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with mechanical, electrical, and software teams to validate system performance and establish effective, reliable acceptance testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support contract manufacturers&#39; builds through final integration and test to consistently deliver conformant hardware to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply DFM/DFX principles and provide feedback to design engineering on assigned equipment and assemblies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support equipment deployment, including installation, validation, and commissioning, ensuring production readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor process and equipment performance, using metrics and data to drive continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own project deliverables with minimum guidance, escalating appropriately when scope is ambiguous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel between Emeryville and Santa Clara sites as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in manufacturing engineering, with exposure to automation and equipment design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting or implementing automated systems in a production environment (robotics is a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in semiconductor, solar, Biotech, EV, or similar high-tech industries, with an understanding of their processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in CAD software (e.g., SolidWorks, AutoCAD, Onshape) for equipment design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with manufacturing/production processes, from assembly drawing through to running hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of manufacturing processes, such as machining, assembly, welding, or material handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with lean manufacturing principles and Six Sigma methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Product Lifecycle Management (PLM) systems (Arena software a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with document control and release processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and analytical skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good communication and collaboration abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage a project with minimum guidance and prioritize tasks effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A first-principles mindset — you question assumptions and approach problems with a foundational understanding rather than relying solely on precedent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of basic coding: RSLogix, Ignition, Python, or C/C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
