&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Mechanical Engineer to invent and build precision machinery for our Matter Compiler™ platform. You’ll turn demanding process requirements into automated machines, developing robotics and equipment for laser micromachining, deposition, fluid handling, and bonding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own designs from early concepts through qualification and deployment, working alongside experienced engineers who will challenge your thinking and help you grow. Our in-house labs, machine shop, and Hybrid Fab give you the tools to build, test, and refine your ideas quickly and see your machines operate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conceive, design, build, and qualify precision mechanisms, robotic axes, end effectors, and process hardware that enable new manufacturing capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from first principles to solve coupled problems in mechanics, thermal behavior, and process physics, balancing precision, throughput, and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and instrument prototypes, test your predictions, and investigate unexpected results. Carry what you learn through design improvements, qualification, and deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with electrical, software, and process engineers to integrate motion, sensing, controls, and mechanical hardware into complete machines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce clear CAD models, drawings, BOMs, and technical documentation that let others build, test, and maintain your designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years designing and building complex mechanical or mechatronic systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering fundamentals and depth in at least one area such as machine design, precision engineering, thermal systems, fluids, or materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in CAD, mechanical drawings, and tolerancing, with practical knowledge of manufacturing processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience fabricating, assembling, testing, and debugging hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity to explore unfamiliar technical problems, initiative to develop and test ideas, and willingness to seek feedback and follow through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. in Mechanical Engineering or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-vacuum equipment, laser or optical systems, precision robotics, or fluid and electrochemical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
