&lt;h3&gt;About The Role:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;You’ll lead Vacuum Systems mechanical engineering and build the team and capabilities needed to expand the Matter Compiler’s manufacturing processes. Your immediate priority is our physical vapor deposition (PVD) system.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;The work spans vacuum chambers and pumping, deposition sources, precision motion, thermal management, and automated material handling. You’ll own development from concept through qualification and sustained operation.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;This is a hands-on leadership role. You’ll set architecture with technical leads, review designs, guide experiments, and resolve integration problems with process, electrical, controls, software, and manufacturing partners.You’ll develop engineers and technical leaders, establish engineering standards, and set priorities for the Vacuum Systems team. An engineering program manager will partner with you on planning, dependencies, and delivery.
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problems You’ll Solve&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate process and device requirements into equipment that meets throughput, repeatability, reliability, and cost targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and qualify a high-rate PVD system, balancing deposition performance with vacuum, thermal, handling, and maintenance constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Choose what to buy, adapt, or develop in house, using proven designs and focused experiments to shorten development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish performance across representative operating conditions, maintenance cycles, and repeated builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build, Own, Drive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build.&lt;/strong&gt; Hire missing expertise and develop engineers and leaders who can independently own difficult technical work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own.&lt;/strong&gt; Set technical direction, resolve system interfaces, and hold the team accountable for equipment performance and readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive.&lt;/strong&gt; Prioritize technical risks, allocate people and resources, and make commitments grounded in analysis, experiments, and build progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast learning loops. Our in-house labs, machine shop, and build team support early testing. The Hybrid Fab connects equipment decisions to process and device results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First principles and experience. We combine proven engineering practices with analysis and experiments, testing assumptions as requirements change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System in the loop. We verify repeatable performance in operation, including recovery after service and faults.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecasts informed by evidence. We retire risks early and update plans as measurements change our understanding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Need:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical leadership developing PVD equipment or substantial PVD modules through integration, commissioning, and qualification, with the system breadth to guide a complete tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong mechanical and vacuum engineering fundamentals: chamber design, pumping and gas loads, precision motion, thermal management, materials compatibility, and verification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience adapting industry designs and practices to new requirements, with demonstrated improvements in development time or equipment performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct engineering management experience: hiring, developing independent technical ownership, addressing performance, and delivering across disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideally Your Background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery of complex vacuum equipment beyond the initial prototype into qualified operation and subsequent builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on architecture, design review, testing, and root-cause analysis, including work with suppliers and service teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building the integration capabilities, engineering standards, and review practices needed by a growing equipment organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting direction, developing leaders, and making resource, supplier, or architecture decisions across programs or equipment generations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. in Mechanical Engineering or a related discipline, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
