&lt;h3&gt;About The Role:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Manager, Platform Manufacturing Engineering to lead Production Manufacturing Engineering as we scale the Matter Compiler from pilot production into high-volume manufacturing. You will own the equipment that builds our devices — its build, integration, bring-up, qualification and reliability — and the team of engineers who deliver it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are an engineer first.&lt;/strong&gt; This is a player-coach role and the player half is not decorative: you will spearhead the hardest projects on the critical path personally, in CAD and on the floor, and use that work as the vehicle for coaching everyone around you. The fastest way to set a standard here is to define it while you produce work that meets it, then mentor your team to achieve the same bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mentoring here happens inside the work, not alongside it. You will pull engineers onto the projects you lead, hand off scope as they are ready for it, review their designs with real technical depth, and grow the next set of project leads out of people who learned by building with you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The management half is real. You will hire against a plan rather than a wish list, develop engineers toward the next level, run performance honestly, and install the operating standards this function works to — documentation, change control, qualification and release discipline, and what &quot;done&quot; means before work leaves the group. You will plan the organization ahead of where the business is today, own headcount and capital budget, and get manufacturability and equipment requirements into specifications set by other teams rather than reviewing them at the end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spearhead the hardest equipment projects on the critical path yourself — architecture, CAD, build, bring-up and qualification — and bring engineers along on them as the primary way they develop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of 5–10 engineers spanning equipment design, automation and controls, integration, and sustaining, through a mix of direct reports and technical leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the engineering standard by producing work to it: reference designs, qualification plans, RCCAs and documentation your team can pattern from, with the reasoning made explicit so it transfers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach through the work — pair on designs, run technical reviews with real depth, hand off scope as engineers are ready for it, and grow the next set of project leads out of people who built alongside you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the delivery record for the function — the equipment, qualifications and production readiness your team commits to, against committed dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead equipment deployment end to end: installation, validation, commissioning, acceptance testing, SOP/WI release and operator qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run root cause and corrective action personally on the failures that matter, teach the method by doing it in front of the team, and drive the corrective actions across teams that do not report to you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install and uphold the operating standards: documentation, change control, qualification and release discipline, RCCA method and closure, and how work is reviewed before it leaves the group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan organizational growth — forecast hiring needs ahead of demand, define roles and levels, build and defend the hiring plan, and manage headcount and capital budget with Supply Chain and Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and resolve escalated personnel situations arising from business and priority changes, rather than routing them away.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get manufacturability and equipment requirements into specification setting and design milestones with Design Engineering and Product, rather than reviewing at the end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance competing priorities with peer leaders so committed deliverables are still met, and own communication of impact and resolution path where they cannot be.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own contract manufacturer and automation supplier execution through final integration and test to conformant hardware on schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive throughput, yield, cost and uptime improvement — held with control limits, not delivered as one-time gains — and establish the operating metrics and reporting cadence leadership can rely on without chasing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel between Emeryville and Santa Clara sites as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Need:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of manufacturing or equipment engineering experience, including 3+ years managing engineers with 5 or more direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current hands-on capability.&lt;/strong&gt; You still design in CAD, still debug hardware on the floor, and could take the hardest open task on your team&#39;s board tomorrow. We will test this directly in the loop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ownership of automated production equipment end to end — architecture through mechanical, controls and software integration, into a qualified, released system running in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in CAD for equipment design (SolidWorks, Onshape, AutoCAD or similar), with recent personal use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of &lt;strong&gt;developing engineers through the work&lt;/strong&gt; — specific people who grew because you put them on projects you were leading, reviewed their designs, and handed off scope as they were ready for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building out a functional group: defining roles, hiring against a plan, and installing the operating standards — not only inheriting an existing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a team spanning more than one discipline (e.g., equipment, controls/automation, integration, sustaining), including people whose work sits outside your own background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership of headcount and capital budget, with resourcing tradeoff decisions made under real constraint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Depth across DFx, RCCA, eBOM→mBOM conversion, qualification and acceptance testing, and PLM/document control and release (Arena a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in semiconductor, solar, hardware-based biotech, EV, or similar high-tech industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence cross-functionally without authority — specifically, getting manufacturing and equipment requirements into specifications owned by other teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A first-principles mindset — you question assumptions, reframe problems from the ground up, and approach challenges with a foundational understanding rather than relying solely on precedent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field; advanced degree preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Bonus Points For:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up or rebuilding a manufacturing or equipment engineering function at a company moving from pilot to production scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience staying technically current while managing — a design, patent, or build you personally delivered while running a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of basic coding: RSLogix, Ignition, Python, or C/C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The compensation for this position also includes equity and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$250,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt; Atomic Machines is an equal opportunity employer that values diversity and does not discriminate based on characteristics protected by applicable law. We are committed to an inclusive interview experience, including for individuals with disabilities. To request an accommodation, contact&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:rc@atomicmachines.com&quot;&gt; rc@atomicmachines.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;To help our recruiting team manage application volume and respond to candidates more efficiently, Atomic Machines may use AI-assisted tools. &lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div data-qa=&quot;job-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atomic Machines is building the Matter Compiler™, the first in a new class of AI-native, all-digital manufacturing systems that build working machines directly from code. The Matter Compiler&amp;nbsp; (MC) is aimed at micro-machines: motors and gears the size of a grain of sand, robots small enough to work inside the body, cooling built directly into the chips that run AI, and the many devices like them that have been waiting on a way to build them. Its first product is PrimeSwitch™, an electromechanical power relay the size of a button battery that carries 150 amps continuous current and opens in 50 microseconds, about a thousand times faster than a conventional contactor. Founded by Jeff Holden — serial entrepreneur, ex-Amazon SVP and Uber’s first Chief Product Officer — the company has raised $250 million to date.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atomic Machines is based in the San Francisco Bay Area, with offices in Emeryville and Santa Clara.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About The Role:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a broad-responsibility, high-judgment team leader role within the IT team. The Senior Manager, Network and Information Security is a strategic leadership role responsible for architecting, building, and governing the enterprise network and security infrastructure across a high-tech manufacturing environment. This role blends deep technical expertise in network architecture, cloud networking, and cybersecurity with people management to develop and lead a small team of engineers and vendor resources to deliver secure, resilient, and scalable connectivity across all production and corporate sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position serves as the principal authority on network and security, working cross-functionally with IT, engineering, and business stakeholders to align network capabilities with manufacturing operational goals. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a full-time, onsite position based in either our Emeryville or Santa Clara office, with occasional work from the other office as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership, Team and Vendor Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly supervise, mentor, and develop a very small team of network and security engineers, providing technical guidance, and career development for internal members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set team priorities, manage workloads, and ensure 24/7 network operational coverage through effective on-call rotation and escalation protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of continuous improvement, knowledge sharing, and operational excellence within the network security team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, onboard, and retain top networking and security talent aligned with the organization&#39;s growth roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage external network and security vendors, holding all parties accountable to defined SLAs, quality standards, and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network Architecture and Design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and own the end-to-end enterprise network architecture strategy, including LAN/WAN, SD-WAN, wireless, interconnects, and OT/IT segmentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect scalable, high-availability network solutions that support manufacturing operations, IoT devices, and enterprise applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and recommend emerging network technologies, vendors, and platforms to address capability gaps and future-state requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain comprehensive network architecture drawings, topology diagrams, standards documentation, and lifecycle roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead routing and switching design, including BGP, OSPF, VLAN segmentation, QoS, and equipment lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS Cloud Networking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and manage AWS networking constructs including VPCs, Transit Gateways, Direct Connect, VPN connections, Security Groups, and NACLs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect hybrid connectivity between on-premises manufacturing sites and AWS cloud environments, ensuring low-latency, secure, and resilient integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and DevOps teams to define and enforce network guardrails, tagging standards, and AWS Organizations-level networking policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize AWS networking costs and performance through right-sizing, traffic engineering, and architectural reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network Security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and enforcement of network security policies, including firewall rule management, zero-trust network access (ZTNA), network access control (NAC), and micro-segmentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee network vulnerability assessments and penetration test scoping; ensure timely remediation and deliver clear risk assessment reports to stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the installation, configuration, and lifecycle of firewalls, IDS/IPS, proxies, and related security appliances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compliance activities (e.g., NIST, SOC 2, ISO 27001, etc.) through network controls documentation, audit evidence, and remediation execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create management processes to keep all network equipment current and hardened against known vulnerabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with team members to facilitate Purple Team and Table Top Exercises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operations &amp;amp; Incident Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead day-to-day network operations, ensuring high availability, performance, and reliability across all enterprise and manufacturing network segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve break/fix incidents on network security systems, serving as the senior technical escalation point for both internal engineers and external vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee network monitoring platforms (e.g., Grafana, Datadog, LogicMonitor, etc); define alerting thresholds, dashboards, and response runbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead incident response for high-severity network outages, serving as the escalation point from the 24/7 operational support team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive root cause analysis (RCA) investigations; author and publish detailed RCA reports and corrective action plans for senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage ticketing workflows, ensuring SLA adherence for network-related work orders and user-reported issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder Collaboration &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary network engineering liaison to IT leadership, OT engineering, manufacturing operations, and engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in capacity planning, capital expenditure budgeting, and vendor contract negotiations for network infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present network strategy, risk posture, and project updates to IT leadership and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Need:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive network engineering experience, with at least 3 years in a people management or technical lead role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience architecting enterprise-grade network solutions in a manufacturing, industrial, or highly regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on experience with AWS networking services (VPC, Transit Gateway, Direct Connect, Route 53, WAF, Security Groups).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in network security device management including NGFWs (Palo Alto, Fortinet, Cisco), IDS/IPS, NAC, CASB/SASE, and Web Filtering platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in routing and switching protocols: BGP, OSPF, EIGRP, MSTP, VLANs, and QoS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with wireless network design and management (Cisco Meraki, Aruba, or equivalent) across large, distributed campuses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification(s) in CCNP Enterprise or CCIE, AWS Certified Advanced Networking – Specialty, CISSP or CISM, Palo Alto PCNSE, AWS Solutions Architect – Professional, ITIL v4 Foundation, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Network Engineering, or related field. Equivalent experience considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Technical Skills:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network platforms Cisco (IOS-XE/XR/NX-OS), Palo Alto, Juniper, Meraki, Fortinet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud Networking: AWS VPC, Transit Gateway, Direct Connect, VPN, WAF, Security Groups, NACLs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security Tools: Firewalls, IDS/IPS, SIEM (Rapid7/Splunk/Palo Alto), NAC (Cisco FrISE/Aruba ClearPass), Vulnerability Scanners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protocols: BGP, OSPF, EIGRP, STP/MSTP, VXLAN, DMVPN, MPLS, 802.1x, QoS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wireless: Enterprise Wi-Fi 6/6E, WPA3, WLAN controllers, RF design and site surveys&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
