&lt;h3&gt;About The Role:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Senior Technical Recruiter who is outstanding at the fundamentals and can find extraordinary talent, earn the attention of passive candidates, create an exceptional candidate experience, and consistently close high-impact hires. Beyond that, we’re looking for someone who thrives in the pace and ambiguity of an early-stage company and is excited to build alongside some of the brightest engineers, scientists, and business leaders in the industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll partner directly with hiring managers as a trusted advisor, helping shape hiring strategies, challenge assumptions, and influence decisions. From defining the ideal candidate profile to sourcing, interviewing, and creating a thoughtful candidate experience, you’ll own the search end-to-end while helping build the teams that will shape the future of Atomic Machines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re energized by solving difficult hiring problems, working with brilliant people, and having a direct impact on a company that’s disrupting an entire industry, we’d love to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read job descriptions and quickly identify, source, and engage the most relevant candidates in the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write compelling outreach messages that generate responses from passive candidates and build genuine interest in Atomic Machines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver an exceptional candidate experience by keeping candidates informed, gathering and sharing feedback, and ensuring every interaction reflects the company positively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain regular communication with hiring managers on pipeline health, progress, and search challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify when role requirements or candidate profiles need to evolve based on market realities and recommend adjustments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive referrals by engaging employees and partnering with hiring managers as active sourcing contributors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply a consistently high hiring bar using first-principles thinking and role-specific requirements rather than relying on pedigree or brand-name experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Need:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience recruiting for technical roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep fluency with LinkedIn Recruiter and at least one additional sourcing platform (Juicebox, Metaview, Gem, Findem, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build sourcing pipelines for a variety of&amp;nbsp; hard-to-fill software and hardware technical roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of AI tools as a sourcing accelerator (ChatGPT, Claude, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing candidate relationships with proactive, transparent communication throughout the hiring process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment to recognize when a search strategy is not working and confidence to recommend course corrections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to partner closely with hiring managers on pipeline strategy, referrals, and candidate calibration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A first-principles approach to candidate evaluation, focused on role requirements rather than résumé prestige.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work onsite in Emeryville or Santa Clara three days per week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The compensation for this position also includes equity and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$160,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$190,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt; Atomic Machines is an equal opportunity employer that values diversity and does not discriminate based on characteristics protected by applicable law. We are committed to an inclusive interview experience, including for individuals with disabilities. To request an accommodation, contact&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:rc@atomicmachines.com&quot;&gt; rc@atomicmachines.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;To help our recruiting team manage application volume and respond to candidates more efficiently, Atomic Machines may use AI-assisted tools. &lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

